  "summary": "Lightwell Security Advisory: netty-codec 4.1.100.Final-rhlw-00001",
  "details": "Red Hat Lightwell has released io.netty:netty-codec 4.1.100.Final-rhlw-00001 with backported fixes for CVE-2025-58057, CVE-2026-42583, and CVE-2026-59901.\n\nCVE-2025-58057: Netty's BrotliDecoder is vulnerable to DoS via zip bomb style attack\n\nCVE-2026-42583: Netty: Lz4FrameDecoder resource exhaustion\n\nCVE-2026-59901: Netty Bzip2Decoder: Infinite Loop in RLE State Machine Leads to Event-Loop Thread Hang\n\nThis patched artifact is a drop-in replacement for io.netty:netty-codec 4.1.100.Final from Maven Central.",
